Description: Let a palette set the selection highlight colours.
 Ptyxis palettes can set the foreground, background, cursor and the sixteen indexed colours but
 not the selection highlight, so selected text uses the toolkit default. vte exposes the colours
 through vte_terminal_set_color_highlight and vte_terminal_set_color_highlight_foreground.
 .
 Highlight and HighlightForeground are read exactly as the cursor colours are, with
 HighlightBackground accepted as a synonym for Highlight in the same way CursorBackground is for
 Cursor. Both are optional: a palette that omits them leaves the alpha at zero, which is the
 same "not set" test the cursor handling uses, so every existing palette is unaffected.
